Cell["\<\
A notebook-only roadmap of the carrier, field update, local rewrite, and \
quotient dynamics.  The four numbered objects use different state spaces and \
transition conventions.\
\>", "Caption",
 ShowCellBracket->False,
 CellMargins->{{84, 84}, {2, 18}},
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|"Suppressed" -> "True"|>, 
   "GoGNotebook" -> <|
    "PresentationOnly" -> True, "ID" -> "GoGVisualAbstractCaption"|>|>,
 FontSlant->Plain,
 FontColor->RGBColor[0.37, 0.42, 0.49],
 CellTags->{
  "GoGNotebookVisual", 
   "GoGVisualAbstractCaption"},ExpressionUUID->"bc23d19c-9e00-f72e-7e4a-\
9b29bf5bdf92"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"V", "(", "f", ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
   RowBox[{
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", "i"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["f", "i"], "-", 
       OverscriptBox["f", "_"]}], ")"}], "2"]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|
    "SourceTeX" -> "\\[\n  \\V(f)=\\sum_i(f_i-\\bar f)^2\n\\]", "Separator" -> 
     "\n"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->"130bb503-5e0c-a2aa-5d85-8293c1965907"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "then decreases by exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["1", "2"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["f", "i"], "-", 
       SubscriptBox["f", "j"]}], ")"}], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "(f_i-f_j)^2/2"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"bc5b6aef-1dda-f505-6eb1-ac8bbc160b5a"],
 ".  Identifying an unlabelled target\nwith a chosen representative only \
permutes the field coordinates and does not\nchange this identity."
}], "Abstract",
 CellDingbat->None,
 TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"Separator" -> "\n\n"|>|>,
 CellFrameLabels->{{None, None}, {None, None}},
 CounterIncrements->{},
 FontSlant->Plain,ExpressionUUID->"12cd61b2-2227-fd03-a420-d425da3b904c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the local-first walk, called Rule A, every one of the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"3", " ", "N"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "3N"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->
  "6acbc9cf-a7ed-9512-5949-43f8ff27a313"],
 " edge-resolution\nslots is equally likely.  We prove that its stationary \
distribution is the\nconnected cubic configuration model projected to \
unlabelled graph classes.\nFor every adapted sequence of connected carriers, \
the logarithm of the largest\npossible nonconstant-field norm, divided by the \
number of steps, is at most\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"O", "(", 
     FractionBox["1", 
      SuperscriptBox["N", "5"]], ")"}], "-", 
    FractionBox[
     SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], 
     RowBox[{"6", " ", 
      SuperscriptBox["N", "3"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|
   "MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "-\\pi^2/(6N^3)+O(N^{-5})"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"762abec7-7431-4b74-444a-de46838e4053"],
 ".  Under the Rule-A stationary law,\nthe random-cubic expansion theorem \
improves this bound to\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", 
       RowBox[{"o", "(", "1", ")"}]}], "-", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", 
       SqrtBox["2"]}], "+", "3"}], 
     RowBox[{"6", " ", "N"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|
   "MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "-(3-2\\sqrt2-o(1))/(6N)"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"049de847-48b0-cd2c-ad20-cf35749000d2"],
 ".  These are field-contraction statements, not mixing\nestimates for the \
graph-valued walk.  For that base walk, the cut between\nbridged and \
bridgeless classes has conductance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"2", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"o", "(", "1", ")"}], "+", "1"}], ")"}]}], 
    RowBox[{"3", " ", "N"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "2/(3N)(1+o(1))"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"6be4a4b2-1956-3a1c-e529-40cb68c7e1c2"],
 ", so its\nrelaxation and total-variation mixing times are at least linear \
in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["N", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "N"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->
  "9a3ae36f-2d6f-c1b2-64d8-7b3e83bd65fb"],
 "."
}], "Abstract",
 CellDingbat->None,
 TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"Separator" -> "\n\n"|>|>,
 CellFrameLabels->{{None, None}, {None, None}},
 CounterIncrements->{},
 FontSlant->Plain,ExpressionUUID->"71b59ac0-1556-f57b-37c0-29e4fd63f4bf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For Rule B, each distinct nonself quotient neighbour receives probability\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["1", 
    RowBox[{"3", " ", "N"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "1/(3N)"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"f1c09542-1fb3-20a4-82d9-ae156ea65394"],
 " and the unused probability is assigned to holding.  This fixed clock\nis \
symmetric, has the uniform class law as its stationary distribution, and\nits \
operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "I-P_B"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"71077e40-eba5-73d0-4f91-6f9a93297cbf"],
 " equals the simple-support Laplacian divided by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"3", " ", "N"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "3N"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f23e370-a5cd-a390-2a1a-5c78a706b06f"],
 ".  It\navoids normalizing by the uncontrolled number of neighbours.  A \
Rule-B field\nprocess additionally requires a choice of concrete move above \
each quotient\ntransition.  Once all\nsuch moves receive positive \
probability, the fields with zero one-step\nvariance loss are exactly those \
that are constant on each component of the\ncarrier formed by active edges.  \
It remains open to prove a positive lower\nbound for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Lambda]", "2"], "(", 
    SubscriptBox["L", "supp"], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|
   "MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "\\lambda_2(L_{\\rm supp})"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"229622e5-535b-7c32-c51a-52a36d34fd80"],
 " and to determine the long-time contraction\nof any specified Rule-B field \
lift."
}], "Abstract",
 CellDingbat->None,
 TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"Separator" -> "\n\n"|>|>,
 CellFrameLabels->{{None, None}, {None, None}},
 CounterIncrements->{},
 FontSlant->Plain,ExpressionUUID->"5c21e517-17aa-d63f-3f6b-8d5410ee5eae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On the persistent labelled process, exact finite-time consensus occurs at\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["N", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "2"}], ",", "4", ",", "8"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "N=2,4,8"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"2359003d-7013-d4ed-f520-e44ecb0d6c8c"],
 ".  Complete unlabelled enumeration through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"N", "\[LongEqual]", "14"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "N=14"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"87647369-3dde-18fe-94c9-16dc157f3fad"],
 " checks the finite\ncounts, spectra, bridge cut, and Rule-B \
zero-contraction classes without\npromoting those finite observations to \
asymptotic theorems."
}], "Abstract",
 CellDingbat->None,
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|
    "EnvironmentClose" -> "\n\\end{abstract}", "Separator" -> "\n\n"|>|>,
 CounterIncrements->{},
 FontSlant->Plain,ExpressionUUID->"71b162e6-3fce-f6b2-4005-c415b8969caa"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Introduction and contributions", "Section",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|
    "Indent" -> "", "Trailing" -> "", "Separator" -> "\n\n"|>|>,
 FontSlant->Plain,ExpressionUUID->"5f35dd6c-8a84-f4d5-df84-a1a49f7eaf83"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Fix an even integer ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["N", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "N"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d138586-cfc8-65be-d705-dc0807b279a2"],
 ". Let ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["C", "N"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "\\C_N"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"6b59618e-bca7-f752-bd5f-bf5312386ed5"],
 " be the finite set of connected cubic\nmultigraphs on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["N", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "N"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->
  "fd38d176-1f3d-f47b-b75a-22cc752b859c"],
 " vertices, considered up to isomorphism unless labels are\nexplicitly \
introduced. Loops and multiple edges are allowed; a loop contributes\ntwo to \
the degree. In addition to the carrier graph itself, there are three\n\
graph-of-graphs conventions on this material. Li's labelled simple graph has\n\
fixed-labelled cubic graphs as vertices and collapses repeated moves to the\n\
same labelled target.  Grave de Peralta--Kolpakov's directed multigraph has\n\
unlabelled classes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"[", 
    StyleBox["G", "TI"], "]"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "[G]"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->
  "4aea28dc-adcd-e5d5-9091-05f101cf3a73"],
 " as vertices and retains one directed slot for each\nunlabelled Whitehead \
resolution, including multiplicity and self-slots.\nFinally, the unlabelled \
simple-support graph has the same class vertices but\ncollapses all positive \
nonself multiplicities to one undirected edge. We use\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "N"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "\\G_N"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"1756d047-4387-2018-8a76-988db747e1c9"],
 " only when the accompanying text specifies the edge convention; every\n\
degree, Laplacian, stationary law, and ball is indexed by its underlying\n\
object."
}], "Text",
 TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"Separator" -> "\n\n"|>|>,
 FontSlant->Plain,ExpressionUUID->"3e5f699e-7cac-a431-6abb-c20b62b7d66c"],

Cell["\<\
The four state-and-clock conventions used below are summarized as follows.\
\>", "Text",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|
    "Separator" -> "\n", "BibliographyTeX" -> 
     "The four state-and-clock conventions used below are summarized as \
follows.\n{\\small"|>|>,
 FontSlant->Plain,ExpressionUUID->"5f43910f-72ec-9465-63f5-71e9fdaf4647"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  InterpretationBox[Cell[BoxData[
    FormBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
        {
         InterpretationBox[Cell[BoxData[
           FormBox[
