     "\\[\n    \\kappa(p,q)=\\norm{T_p-T_q}_{\\mathrm{op}}.\n\\]", 
     "Separator" -> 
     "\n"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->"5aa9c705-8b26-d7ad-20d4-64bec409e2d2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The elementary operators ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["A", "ij"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "A_{ij}"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"0a783c59-e975-1419-08ba-86d57e9f6cb2"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"i", "j"}], "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "I-A_{ij}"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"c60e3400-18b4-8645-cedf-e74c6df987a5"],
 " are projections, not\ndifferentials.  The displayed ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["D", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "D"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->
  "67b24f8d-237c-6cd9-be2f-d39c4965f857"],
 " is currently defined only from vertices to\nedges.  Calling the square \
defect the obstruction to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["D", "2"], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "D^2=0"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"800cee8d-5a78-7cb5-3969-81d1d4df76b8"],
 " would require a\nseparate extension of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["D", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "D"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c27b208-d111-0fa1-be94-4997eea114b0"],
 " from edges to chosen ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["2", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "2"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->
  "fecf0e2a-8adb-2887-eb79-ec7718f7854d"],
 "-cells; without that extra\ndefinition, the justified statement is gauge \
covariance of the path\ndifference."
}], "Text",
 TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"Separator" -> "\n\n"|>|>,
 FontSlant->Plain,ExpressionUUID->"c579677e-6fa3-38bb-ac7d-e26fdd1cb9ac"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "There is already a one-dimensional backtracking defect.  If a Whitehead \
move\non ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["e", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "e"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->
  "11246140-b3a2-045b-48ce-81e224231a3a"],
 " is followed by its graph inverse with coherent inverse settlement, then\n\
in the original frame"
}], "Text",
 TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"Separator" -> "\n"|>|>,
 FontSlant->Plain,ExpressionUUID->"30553b01-2ad8-8f0b-4ee2-a8be0dc6f932"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
       RowBox[{"-", "1"}]]], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["e", "TI"]], "\[NotEqual]", 
    StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], ","}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|
    "SourceTeX" -> "\\[\n    T_{m^{-1}}T_m=A_e^2=A_e\\ne I,\n\\]", 
     "Separator" -> 
     "\n"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->"5d26578d-3a9d-bfc4-67fc-f2b7392721ea"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["e", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "I-A_e"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"ebe14088-b42a-db5b-a8f4-4cb86d304d24"],
 " is a rank-one orthogonal projection of operator norm one.  Thus\neven a \
contractible move--inverse path is dissipative."
}], "Text",
 TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"Separator" -> "\n\n"|>|>,
 FontSlant->Plain,ExpressionUUID->"487a05a2-b5c3-d4f1-dff0-ac07ae6d56a1"],

Cell["\<\
If two concrete Whitehead moves are performed on non-loop edges whose \
endpoint
sets are disjoint, then the corresponding labelled square defect is zero.  \
Any
coherently settled unlabelled square has\
\>", "Proposition",
 CellDingbat->Cell[
   TextData[{"Proposition ", 
     CounterBox["Theorem"], "."}], FontWeight -> "Bold", FontSlant -> "Plain"],
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|
    "Environment" -> "proposition", "EnvironmentOpen" -> 
     "\\begin{proposition}[Flatness for disjoint moves]", "Trailing" -> "", 
     "BodyIndent" -> "\n", "Separator" -> "\n"|>|>,
 CounterIncrements->"Theorem",
 FontSlant->Plain,ExpressionUUID->"eaf5eedd-f8c1-291b-64f8-e2addb55dee5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"S", "p", "e", "c"}], "TI"], 
     StyleBox["sing",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "-", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["q", "TI"]]}], ")"}]}], "\[LongEqual]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", "0"}], "}"}], "."}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|
    "SourceTeX" -> "\\[\n    \\Specsing(T_p-T_q)=\\{0,\\ldots,0\\}.\n\\]", 
     "EnvironmentClose" -> "\n\\end{proposition}", "Separator" -> 
     "\n\n"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->"0022c284-6f13-38ec-d16f-74488523d5e1"],

Cell["\<\
In the half-edge model, each Whitehead move only reassigns the four \
half-edges
incident to the endpoints of the selected edge and not belonging to that \
edge.
Disjoint endpoint sets give disjoint local data, so the graph rewrites commute.
The field operators also commute because the averaging projections act on
disjoint coordinate pairs.  Thus both two-step path transports are identical,
up to the same final settlement.\
\>", "Proof",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|
    "Environment" -> "proof", "EnvironmentOpen" -> "\\begin{proof}", 
     "Trailing" -> "", "BodyIndent" -> "\n", "EnvironmentClose" -> 
     "\n\\end{proof}", "Separator" -> "\n\n"|>|>,
 FontSlant->Plain,ExpressionUUID->"e905b943-db18-3548-5c51-341c77eeb831"],

Cell["\<\
Incident squares are the basic non-flat squares.  Their defect is not only a
property of the cubic graph rewrite; it also includes the averaging \
operators.
Locally, when the two consecutive averaged pairs share one vertex, the
commutator has singular values\
\>", "Text",
 TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"Separator" -> "\n"|>|>,
 FontSlant->Plain,ExpressionUUID->"e6f8693b-9a2b-b775-e53b-9c10cca5a6af"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    SqrtBox["3"], "4"], ",", 
   FractionBox[
    SqrtBox["3"], "4"], ",", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|
    "SourceTeX" -> "\\[\n    \\frac{\\sqrt3}{4},\\frac{\\sqrt3}{4},0\n\\]", 
     "Separator" -> 
     "\n"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->"a40d534e-1758-d1fb-01bd-8d978ee7f135"],

Cell["\<\
on the three affected coordinates.  In an actual GoG square this local \
algebra
is dressed by the two graph rewrites and the endpoint settlements.\
\>", "Text",
 TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"Separator" -> "\n\n"|>|>,
 FontSlant->Plain,ExpressionUUID->"b0c1089b-7183-003f-96b5-33f938f26571"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Automorphisms create one extra subtlety.  If the endpoint graph has a \
nontrivial\nautomorphism group, two apparently different final settlements \
may differ by\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"U", "\[Element]", 
    RowBox[{"Aut", " ", "\[Delta]"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  TaggingRules-><|
   "MathNotebook" -> <|"SourceTeX" -> "U\\in\\Aut(\\delta)"|>|>,
  ExpressionUUID->"8d5b155b-a0ee-d42d-da00-9fee3d2f6df2"],
 ".  A quotient-level aligned defect is therefore"
}], "Text",
 TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"Separator" -> "\n"|>|>,
 FontSlant->Plain,ExpressionUUID->"8dd6e96b-4c14-3ed4-d635-a08aed94500d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Kappa]", 
     StyleBox["orb",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "(", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["q", "TI"]}], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
   RowBox[{
    UnderscriptBox["min", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["U", "TI"], "\[Element]", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox[
        RowBox[{"A", "u", "t"}], "TI"], 
       RowBox[{"(", "\[Delta]", ")"}]}]}],
     LimitsPositioning->True], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "-", 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["q", "TI"]]}]}], 
      StyleBox["op",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], "."}]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|
    "SourceTeX" -> 
     "\\[\n    \\kappa_{\\mathrm{orb}}(p,q)\n    =\n    \
\\min_{U\\in\\Aut(\\delta)}\n    \\norm{T_p-UT_q}_{\\mathrm{op}}.\n\\]", 
     "Separator" -> 
     "\n"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->"835a04d6-4b6d-e937-b40b-a4f44b829d25"],

Cell["\<\
This is not needed when the two lifted paths and settlements are tracked
coherently, but it is useful when comparing defects computed from canonical
representatives.  Averaging over all settlements,\
\>", "Text",
 TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"Separator" -> "\n"|>|>,
 FontSlant->Plain,ExpressionUUID->"e08a15c3-bfbd-e7aa-a161-0c297534eae1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["T", "TI"], "_"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox["1", 
      TemplateBox[{
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["u", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
          RowBox[{"(", "\[Delta]", ")"}]}]},
       "Abs"]], 
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
       RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "\[Element]", 
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox[
          RowBox[{"A", "u", "t"}], "TI"], 
         RowBox[{"(", "\[Delta]", ")"}]}]}],
       LimitsPositioning->True], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["P", "TI"], "\[Alpha]"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}]}]}]}], ","}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "MathNotebook" -> <|
    "SourceTeX" -> 
     "\\[\n    \\overline T_m\n    =\n    \\frac{1}{|\\Aut(\\delta)|}\n    \
\\sum_{\\alpha\\in\\Aut(\\delta)}P_\\alpha T_m,\n\\]", "Separator" -> 
     "\n"|>|>,ExpressionUUID->"9ac86bbb-83f0-5379-337c-386634d9173c"],

Cell["\<\
is canonical but changes the dynamics: it projects toward
automorphism-invariant components and can introduce artificial contraction.\
\>", "Text",
 TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"Separator" -> "\n\n"|>|>,
 FontSlant->Plain,ExpressionUUID->"0b3350b4-ab68-8422-3bc5-27b2538639db"]
}, Open  ]],

