Cell["\<\
Because fixed-clock Rule B has uniform stationary law, its mass column is the
class fraction.  Every zero-gap class in the enumeration is bridged.  The
active-edge theorem makes the zero one-step gaps exact; the table does not
imply a zero long-time field exponent.\
\>", "Text",
 TaggingRules-><|"MathNotebook" -> <|"Separator" -> "\n\n"|>|>,
 FontSlant->Plain,ExpressionUUID->"4d1d931b-c9b7-d171-4d4a-88b88be73d04"]
}, Open  ]],

